(text "REVIEW ONLY / OPAQUE COTS USAGE\nGomSpace A/S / NanoPower BP8 100 Wh (8S1P)\nProduct ID: gomspace-bp8-100wh-8s1p\nPart number: NanoPower BP8 100 Wh (ordering designation, numeric P/N not stated)\nRevision: catalog-record-1; product hardware revision not stated\nAllocated roles: battery. One physical usage record. Quantity: 1.\nAccounting boundary: One complete BP8 pack including cells, protection, balancing, telemetry\nelectronics and heater. EPS/P80, harness, mating connectors and spacecraft structure are external.\nPack electronics and heater mass are not additional installed products.\nSupported catalog configurations (none is automatically chosen):\nFactory 8S1P pack. One pack in this record. Two packs may be paralleled using the manufacturer’s\nwiring and manual. No series reconfiguration inferred.\nSources (exact URLs and document revisions also in manifest.json):\nNanoPower BP8 100 Wh Datasheet / DS 1069134, revision 1.2.0, 2026-04-10\nhttps://gomspace.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/gs-ds-nanopower-bp8-100-Wh-2.pdf\nLocation: Printed pp. 1–13 (PDF pp. 5–17). Tables 2.1–2.2, pp. 5–6. Table 4.1, p. 11.. Retrieved:\n2026-10-17\nCatalog caveats:\n86 Wh is typical over 23.6–32.0 V. It is not guaranteed minimum usable energy and is not an EOL\ncapacity.\nThe 100 Wh and 3.5 Ah headline values use a different/full capacity case. They are retained\nseparately and not substituted into the recommended-range energy field.\nCycle-life domain and aging/efficiency models are missing. Telemetry SoC capability does not supply\na charge-state model for the demo.\nProtection thresholds differ from recommended operating limits. Absolute maxima must not be treated\nas the normal operating interval." (at 25.4 52.07 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left)) (uuid 2ee8ce50-7b2f-4309-86ba-83eed7ddaebf))
